{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_destination_charge", "label": "Stripe Connect destination charge", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chosen so the commission is withheld as application_fee_amount at charge time: collected atomically with the payment, no payout job and no second debit."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_express_connect_account", "label": "Express Connect account (FR)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Capabilities card_payments + transfers so Stripe hosts KYC; business_type is left unset so the hosted form can ask whether the chef is a micro-entreprise or a company."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_commission_bps", "label": "Basis-point commission with frozen rates", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Integer arithmetic avoids float drift, and freezing rate_bps/vat_rate_bps on the commissions row means a later rate change can never rewrite history or break an audit replay."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_payments_bookings_1n", "label": "payments 1:N bookings", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately not 1:1: a failed card attempt must be retryable with a fresh PaymentIntent, so a booking may carry several payment rows and the most recent non-failed row is the live attempt."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_booking_confirm_on_webhook", "label": "Booking confirmed only on payment_intent.succeeded", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The API never trusts the client's confirmation result; only the webhook flips the booking to confirmed."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_sepa_mandate", "label": "SEPA mandate (CORE)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recorded but never debited in the card phase; groundwork for avance immediate and CESU where the fee cannot be split at charge time. Only the IBAN last four digits are persisted; the IBAN itself never reaches the backend."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_sap_declaration", "label": "SAP declaration (sap_profiles)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lives in UsersModule rather than PaymentsModule because it is self-declared profile data carrying no Stripe secrets. type_a_nova vs type_b_cooperative; switching type clears the other type's fields."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_no_self_habilitation", "label": "No self-declared habilitation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "urssafTiersPrestationStatus and crcesuAffiliationStatus are absent from the update DTO by design, the same rule as isActive/isVerified: a chef must not declare themselves habilitated."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_attestation_per_chef", "label": "One fiscal attestation per issuing chef", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Confirmed 2026-09-04: the chef is the declared prestataire, so a single client-level document covering several independent providers would not be valid. Client totals exist for dashboards only."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_cesu_prefinanced", "label": "Prefinanced CESU flow (e-CESU first)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Structurally different from card: the funds never transit through the platform. The client pays the chef directly from the issuer's beneficiary area, so nothing is programmatically verifiable and the commission cannot be withheld at charge time."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_chef_confirms_cesu", "label": "Chef confirms a CESU payment", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No issuer exposes an API and no transaction reference is normalised, so the chef, the only party receiving both the issuer notification and the money, is the confirming authority, with a traced admin force-settle requiring a proof reference for support cases."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_nan_publication", "label": "CRCESU NAN publication", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The NAN must be published on the public chef profile, the booking detail and each quote because a client cannot add the chef on their issuer portal without it, and invoice A arrives far too late to be the sole carrier."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_facture_b", "label": "Commission invoice (facture B)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Issued before any debit because it is the legal basis of the collection: the prelevement is made against the invoice, not against a raw application_fee_amount. Numbered LF-COM-<year>-NNNN; PDF and S3 archival belong to the invoicing workstream."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_commission_debit_engine", "label": "SEPA commission-debit engine", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Webhook-driven because SEPA never answers succeeded synchronously; N attempts per invoice, a 10000 EUR cap, and a recorded clawback window. Deferred out of the card phase and reusable unchanged for the avance immediate."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_no_on_behalf_of_on_debit", "label": "No on_behalf_of on the commission debit", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The platform is the seller on facture B, and on_behalf_of, transfer_data or application_fee_amount would invalidate the already-collected mandate by forcing a fresh authorisation. A dedicated test asserts their absence."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_on_behalf_of_invoice_a", "label": "on_behalf_of for invoice A seller-of-record", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resolved 2026-09-05: adding on_behalf_of to the existing destination charge makes the connected account merchant of record with one parameter, no switch to direct charges. Express chef accounts already hold card_payments, which requires the full service agreement, so no re-onboarding. Not implemented yet."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_invoice_a", "label": "Service invoice A (prestataire-named)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Client-facing, issued in the chef's name by the platform on their behalf, showing the booking's payment method. Trigger is still open: payment_intent.succeeded means charged, not delivered."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_s3_legal_retention", "label": "S3 write-only invoice archival", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "S3 holds only a private copy for the 10-year Code de commerce retention; neither party is ever served from it, so the object key is recorded in Postgres against the owning row."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_sepa_core_scheme", "label": "SEPA CORE scheme constraint", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stripe exposes only the CORE scheme, so the mandat SEPA B2B named in the commercial documentation is not buildable. CORE's no-questions-asked 8-week dispute right is honoured automatically, which drives the reversed state and the booking block."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_clawback_window", "label": "56-day clawback window", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CommissionDebit.clawbackWindowEndsAt models the CORE revocation period as a hard-coded constant, deliberately not configurable: it is the scheme's rule, not the platform's, and a variable invites someone to fix a non-conformity by editing a value."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_webhook_routing_db_lookup", "label": "Webhook routing by database lookup", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never discriminate on metadata: a Dispute carries empty metadata and a Mandate has none, so metadata routing silently misfiles exactly the events that matter. A CommissionDebit lookup on stripePaymentIntentId decides between the commission engine and the client flow."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_stripeeventlog_dedup", "label": "StripeEventLog de-duplication on processedAt", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The guard tests processedAt rather than row existence: a handler that throws has already inserted its row, so an existence check would read Stripe's retry, the one chance to get the event right, as a duplicate and lose it permanently."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_settlepayment", "label": "settlePayment() shared settlement", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Extracted from the card handler as the sole writer of Payment.status succeeded, paidAt and taxCreditEligibleAmount, and owner of the booking transition, which is what makes a mixed CESU + card booking possible."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_mixed_cesu_card", "label": "Mixed CESU + card coverage", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "coverage() counts succeeded payments only, never everything-not-failed, because an abandoned pending row would inflate coverage and a split booking would never reach confirmed. The card intent charges the remaining amount and refuses with 409 when nothing is left."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_partial_unique_index", "label": "Partial unique index on live CESU payments", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "payments (booking_id) WHERE method = cesu AND status <> failed holds concurrency: two simultaneous declarations would each pass the coverage check. Prisma cannot express a partial index, so it exists only in the migration."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_unpaid_commission_guard", "label": "Unpaid-commission guard", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Booking creation and both payment paths refuse 409 for a chef with an invoice out of debit attempts or a commission reversed after a dispute. It is the counterweight to accepting CORE: rather than making an eight-week revocable debit safe, the exposure is capped at what is already owed."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_no_surcharge_rule", "label": "CRCESU no-surcharge rule enforced structurally", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Commission is computed per payment line with no proportional split, a declaration can never exceed what is due, and there is no fee field anywhere on the CESU path."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_paper_cesu_unmanaged", "label": "Paper CESU deliberately unmanaged", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The platform provides the payment method, the invoice and the commission debit; depositing, validating and cashing the titres is the chef's responsibility. No chef-facing contractual document exists yet, so the clause has nowhere to live."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_platform_attested_amount", "label": "platformAttestedAmountCents", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Excludes type B and e-CESU because the issuer already attests the share it financed. Flagged red: the medium is probably not the fiscally relevant axis, and attesting paper may carry the same over-declaration exposure under art. 199 sexdecies CGI. Open with the accountant; the fix is one line in isPlatformAttestable()."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_idempotent_payment_migrations", "label": "Idempotent payments migrations", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "20260831120000 failed mid-file twice during development, once on payment_status and once on payment_method, because Prisma runs migration files outside a transaction; every CREATE is now guarded and every ALTER uses IF EXISTS."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_legacy_payments_deletion", "label": "Legacy payments rows deleted by backfill", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The backfill attaches old rows via bookings.payment_id then bookings.stripe_payment_intent_id; anything matching neither is deleted because booking_id is NOT NULL. Check a production dump before deploying."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_no_scheduler", "label": "No cron scheduler", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The repo has none, and with the debit triggered on confirmation and no titre reimbursement to follow, nothing time-based is mandatory: the monthly batch and debit retries are admin endpoints, advisory-locked for multi-instance Railway."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_sepa_processing_never_succeeded", "label": "sepa_debit PaymentIntents never return succeeded", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "paymentIntents.create on sepa_debit returns processing and a late failure surfaces as requires_payment_method, since a PaymentIntent has no failed status. The API response is therefore only recorded, never trusted."}, {"id": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_migration_not_executed", "label": "CESU migration not executed in the working environment", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No Postgres was reachable, so 20260905120000 must be run against a scratch database before deploying."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_destination_charge", "target": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_commission_bps", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_destination_charge", "target": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_express_connect_account", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_destination_charge", "target": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_booking_confirm_on_webhook", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_payments_bookings_1n", "target": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_destination_charge", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_sepa_mandate", "target": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_destination_charge", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_sap_declaration", "target": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_no_self_habilitation", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_no_self_habilitation", "target": "docs_auth_clerk_integration_contract_chef_vetting", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_attestation_per_chef", "target": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_sap_declaration", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_idempotent_payment_migrations", "target": "docs_database_connection_idempotent_migrations", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-stripe-cb-evolution.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_legacy_payments_deletion", "target": "docs_evolution_payments_stripe_cb_evolution_payments_bookings_1n", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/evolution/payments-st